  logistics: "I-25 north–south and I-70 east–west carry everything. I-70 through the Eisenhower Tunnel and Vail Pass is the single biggest scheduling variable in the state: chain and traction laws apply from September through May, and a closure can add a full day. Denver's older neighborhoods — Capitol Hill, Baker, Highlands — have alley-only access and narrow streets, and downtown high-rises require freight elevator reservations. Above 8,000 feet, expect a shuttle for many properties.",
  seasonal: "June through August is peak and books out early. September and early October are the best window in Colorado: good weather, open availability, and passes still clear. From November through April, any move crossing the Continental Divide carries genuine schedule risk, and we build that into the delivery window rather than promising a date we cannot hold. Spring is the wettest snow season on the Front Range — March blizzards are more common than January ones.",
